  "ood_methodology_clarification": "Maximum Softmax Probability (MSP) confidence thresholding is evaluated against genuine cross-modality medical datasets (e.g. testing dermatology and retinal images against chest models). Benchmark results reveal that deep networks exhibit semantic overconfidence on out-of-domain images, resulting in non-trivial False Accept Rates at default thresholds. Rejection thresholds serve as preliminary triage heuristics, not an absolute out-of-distribution barrier.",
